CloudBurrow patch 51 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1516).

The bug: a RECORD's STRING field, or a REPEATED STRING, that
tables.insert gave a collation ('und:ci') was made in the engine without
it, so its values compared case-sensitively; and the collation of a
STRING inside a STRUCT or an ARRAY column that CREATE TABLE made read
back from tables.get with none.
The fix: CreateTable writes the field's COLLATE inside the column's
STRUCT<...> or ARRAY<...> type, which the engine compares its values by
(googlesqlite patch 0061), and addTableMetadata records the engine's
collation of each nested STRING (nested_collation.go). Its test
server/nested_collation_test.go fails without it.

